& [Review]
  + implementation is a separate bounded crate and does not promote copy or depend on live cantor_scribe
  + the complete assembly envelope and semantic manifest replay before any unit is considered
  + exact and prefix matching use the published lexical lowercase rule and never claim normalization fuzzy relevance or semantic equivalence
  + labels and aliases collapse to one hit per unit while ambiguity between distinct units is preserved
  + dependency visibility kinds namespace context validity status ordering continuation and result identity are explicit and deterministic
  + sealed cursors bind generation filters and continuation coordinates and distinguish stale snapshot from changed query or tamper
  + the instance-contract test admits exactly kernel.sop.semantic-find and proves whole cantor_scribe remains held

& [ThreatReview]
  + strict machine forms reject unknown fields duplicate semantic sets malformed profiles identifiers filters budgets and oversized requests
  + incomplete diagnostic-bearing or tampered assemblies refuse before lookup
  + stale rebound coordinate-tampered cursors and modified result pages fail deterministic replay
  + production dependencies and source contain no filesystem database index async transport process environment network provider CLI unsafe mutation or effect surface
  + retained evidence independently rehashes four artifacts and seven component files before focused replay

& [Residuals]
  + lookup performs a bounded in-memory scan and is not a persistent or full-text index
  + neighborhood completion rule evaluation references search ranking revision drafts SQLite LSP MCP and hosted transport remain separate candidate slices
  + the implementation does not start SOP Eclipse as a process or authorize self-update
  + review is agent-produced and not an independent human audit

& [Disposition]
  + acceptable_for_exact_owned_branch_publication_after_completion_signature_and_attribution
